From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:52:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] RegisterPk: an HJViewer access ticket (field 1001)

HJViewer 1.8.0 is for Yonsei University staff, and its hbbs (server patch
0006) lets a PC go online only with an access ticket that hjv-api signed. The
PC carries it in RegisterPk's new string field hjv_ticket = 1001, in the
1000-1099 range HJViewer keeps for its own fields (as Hash.hjv_nonce and
LoginRequest.hjv_key_proof are). The app does not read the ticket; it sends
it as hjv-api gave it.

An empty string writes no bytes, so a RegisterPk without a ticket is byte for
byte what an app before 1.8.0 sends, and servers that do not check tickets
(upstream, HJViewer's hbbs before 0006 or with the check off) keep field 1001
as an unknown field and act as before. hbbs 0006 reads it as that unknown
field without changing its proto (docs/access-tickets.md 3-2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 protos/rendezvous.proto | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/protos/rendezvous.proto b/protos/rendezvous.proto
index 3cee04e..2a2b5cf 100644
--- a/protos/rendezvous.proto
+++ b/protos/rendezvous.proto
@@ -115,6 +115,9 @@ message RegisterPk {
   bytes pk = 3;
   string old_id = 4;
   bool no_register_device = 5;
+  // HJViewer: field numbers 1000-1099 are HJViewer's; servers built from upstream skip them.
+  // The PC's access ticket, which an HJViewer hbbs checks; empty (no bytes) without one.
+  string hjv_ticket = 1001;
 }
 
 message RegisterPkResponse {
